#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:1
msgid "Agents Usage Tips and Best Practices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:3
msgid ""
"This guide provides practical tips and best practices for getting the "
"most out of your interactions with Mattermost Agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:5
msgid "Voice dictation integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:7
msgid ""
"Enable your operating system's voice dictation or speech recognition "
"tools for hands-free communication with Agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:9
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:11
#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:22
msgid ""
"Start a direct message chat with Agents, and ensure your cursor is in the"
" Mattermost message text box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:12
msgid "Ensure your microphone is connected and working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:13
msgid ""
"Activate Microsoft Voice Typing by pressing the **Windows key + H** to "
"open the voice typing tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:14
msgid "Start talking! Windows transforms your voice into text within Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:16
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:18
msgid ""
"Navigate to **System Settings > Keyboard > Dictation** to enable "
"dictation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:20
msgid "Ensure the Microphone source is set correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:21
msgid "Specify the shortcut key you want to use to turn dictation on and off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:23
msgid ""
"Turn dictation on with the shortcut key you configured, and then start "
"talking! macOS transforms your voice into text within Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:25
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:27
msgid ""
"You'll need an open-source speech recognition tool for Linux, such as "
"Simon, SpeechControl, or Julius. Once you have a speech recognition tool "
"installed and working, enable it, start a direct message with Agents, and"
" start talking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:29
msgid "Best practices for AI interaction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:31
msgid ""
"When working with AI technology like Agents, it's important to understand"
" that the process is often iterative. Using an iterative approach ensures"
" that you leverage Agents to complement your work, leading to higher "
"quality results. Here are some tips for being more effective with Agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:33
msgid "Avoid a one-and-done mindset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:35
msgid ""
"Don't assume that the first output from Agents will be perfect. Instead, "
"review and refine the content to ensure it meets your standards and "
"needs. You can prompt for corrections like \"In the second section, "
"remove mention of widgets\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:37
msgid ""
"Alternatively, use voice memos to prompt for corrections such as \"make "
"edits like \"Remove Section 3\" or \"Switch Section 3 with Section 5\". "
"Reduce unnecessary words by saying \"Remove unnecessary phrases to make "
"this more concise,\" or shorten statements with \"Condense this into a "
"single paragraph\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:39
msgid "Use AI as a tool, not a replacement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:41
msgid ""
"Treat the outputs generated by Agents as initial drafts. Agents can help "
"you enhance your writing and analysis, not replace your own skills and "
"judgment. Think of Agents as your high-tech assistant that can provide "
"suggestions and help you brainstorm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:43
msgid "Iterate for quality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:45
msgid ""
"Go through multiple rounds of revisions to catch errors, improve clarity,"
" and refine the content to better align with your goals. By continually "
"reviewing and tweaking the outputs, you'll end up with more polished and "
"accurate content, and maximize the value of Agents by producing "
"professional-grade results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:47
msgid "Effective prompting techniques"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:49
msgid "Be specific and clear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:51
msgid ""
"The more specific your requests, the better Agents can assist you. "
"Instead of asking \"Help me with this document,\" try \"Review this "
"meeting summary and identify any action items that need follow-up\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:53
msgid "Provide context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:55
msgid ""
"When asking Agents to analyze or work with content, provide relevant "
"background information. This helps the AI understand the purpose and "
"deliver more targeted assistance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:57
msgid "Use follow-up questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:59
msgid ""
"Take advantage of Agents' context memory by asking follow-up questions. "
"If you're working on a project, you can build on previous conversations "
"to refine and improve your work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:61
msgid "Request different perspectives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:63
msgid ""
"Ask Agents to approach problems from different angles or consider various"
" stakeholder viewpoints to get more comprehensive insights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:65
msgid "Workflow integration tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:67
msgid "Start small"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:69
msgid ""
"Begin with simple tasks like summarizing threads or asking basic "
"questions, then gradually incorporate more complex workflows as you "
"become comfortable with the tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:71
msgid "Combine features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:73
msgid ""
"Use multiple Agents features together. For example, search for relevant "
"past discussions, summarize the findings, and then ask Agents to help you"
" synthesize the information into actionable insights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:75
msgid "Document your learnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/usage_tips.md:77
msgid ""
"Keep track of particularly effective prompts or workflows that work well "
"for your team's needs. This helps establish consistent practices across "
"your organization."
msgstr ""

